{"authority":{"artifact":"CANDIDATE_IDENTITY_ONLY","data":"NONE","evidence":"DECLARED_LOCATORS_ONLY_NOT_VERIFIED","execution":"NONE","formation":"NONE","qualification":"NONE","results":"NONE"},"evaluation":{"holdout":"The only unread data is the forward period 2026-10-01T00:00:00Z to 2027-09-30T23:59:59Z, unread when this proposal was frozen. Daily bars of BTC, ETH and SOL through 2026-08 were already observed in exploratory research, so no retrospective period can serve as formation or holdout evidence for this proposal. Any read of the forward period before a separately authorized evaluation, or any change made after observing it, invalidates this proposal.","metrics":[{"id":"metric-1","statement":"Predeclared reject-only diagnostics are per-leg and combined net return after fixed costs, completed round trips, average R per round trip, maximum drawdown, exposure, repair incidence, and unresolved-state count; none is Alpha or qualification evidence."},{"id":"metric-2","statement":"The primary is coordinate 0, entry lookback 50 and exit lookback 20. Coordinates 1 (100, 50) and 2 (20, 10) are nonselectable sensitivities; no sensitivity may replace the primary after observing results."},{"id":"metric-3","statement":"A later effect budget is NOT_GRANTED until a frozen consumable D1 slot count D and source scope are bound; at most one opening and one closing submit per leg per D1 slot, plus one terminal and one drain submit per leg."}]},"evidence":[{"claim":"Exploratory research in research/ronnie/trend: this rule averaged above zero per trade on each of 17 crypto majors over 2018-2026 and +0.33R per trade over 2023-2026, but its lead over random entries with the same exits was not significant at 95% and on coins listed since 2023 it averaged only +0.07R; already observed, so it motivates this proposal and is not formation or holdout evidence.","id":"source-1-exploratory-research","locator":"research/ronnie/trend/majors.txt"},{"claim":"The same exploratory research shows that pullback entries, structure stops, weekly-level targets and a weekly-trend filter did not improve the rule; none is part of this proposal.","id":"source-2-rejected-variants","locator":"research/ronnie/trend/result.txt"},{"claim":"Time-series momentum is a declared design precedent; transfer to BTC, ETH and SOL daily breakouts is unverified and this locator is not evidence of profitability here.","id":"source-3-time-series-momentum","locator":"https://w4.stern.nyu.edu/facdir/lpederse/papers/TimeSeriesMomentum.pdf"},{"claim":"White's Reality Check motivates a reject-only data-snooping policy; the exploratory research behind this proposal tried many families, and the census in research/ronnie/README.md is the multiple-testing record.","id":"source-4-reality-check","locator":"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1111/1468-0262.00152"}],"falsifiers":["Any callback permutation changes the ordered action sequence, terminal state, or fault outcome for identical D1 and H1 facts of the three legs.","Any coordinate, lookback, stop multiple, quantity, metric, or evaluation interval is selected or changed after observing a result.","Any order anomaly cannot be flattened by the one bounded global draining batch or leaves pending or positive residual quantity at the final observation.","BTC or ETH actions change solely because valid SOL values change, or any leg's actions depend on another leg's bars.","The primary coordinate fails a predeclared rejection limit on the forward holdout; the sensitivities cannot rescue it.","The forward holdout is read before separate admission and independently reproducible evaluation."],"hypothesis":"On later-authorized point-in-time forward inputs, a long-flat daily breakout on BTC, ETH and SOL, entering when the daily close exceeds the highest close of the prior 50 days, protected by a stop two Wilder ATR(20) below the average entry fill, and exiting when the daily close falls below the lowest close of the prior 20 days, may support falsifiable fixed-size long-flat behavior; this proposal asserts no Alpha, result, qualification, capacity, live, or execution authority.","identity":"btc-eth-sol-long-flat-daily-breakout-trend-v1","inputs":{"channels":[{"id":"channel-1-btc-d1","statement":"Completed BTC D1 bars (high, low, close) are bound to signal channel 1."},{"id":"channel-2-eth-d1","statement":"Completed ETH D1 bars are bound to signal channel 2; ETH values never enter another leg's calculation."},{"id":"channel-3-sol-d1","statement":"Completed SOL D1 bars are bound to signal channel 3; SOL values never enter another leg's calculation."},{"id":"channel-4-btc-h1","statement":"Completed BTC H1 bars are bound to execution channel 4 and executable handle 1; their low is compared with the BTC stop."},{"id":"channel-5-eth-h1","statement":"Completed ETH H1 bars are bound to execution channel 5 and executable handle 2."},{"id":"channel-6-sol-h1","statement":"Completed SOL H1 bars are bound to execution channel 6 and executable handle 3."},{"id":"channel-7-snapshots","statement":"Every bar callback carries all three executables' position, pending-order and equal balance facts; only a complete H1 triple strictly later than signal availability may consume a daily signal."}]},"kind":"ResearchIntentProposal","non_claims":["NO_ALPHA_CLAIM","NO_DATA_AUTHORITY","NO_EVIDENCE_VERIFICATION","NO_EXECUTION_AUTHORITY","NO_FORMATION_AUTHORITY","NO_LIVE_AUTHORITY","NO_QUALIFICATION_AUTHORITY","NO_RESULT_AUTHORITY","NO_SHORT_AUTHORITY"],"parameter_space":{"parameters":[{"id":"parameter-1-coordinates","statement":"Exactly three stable proposals exist: 0=(entry 50, exit 20), 1=(entry 100, exit 50) and 2=(entry 20, exit 10), each with ATR(20) and a 2.0 ATR stop; no other combination is admitted."},{"id":"parameter-2-signal","statement":"Per leg, enter when close[t] > max(close[t-N..t-1]) with all N prior closes known; exit when close[t] < min(close[t-M..t-1]); both act at the first complete H1 triple strictly after the D1 bar's availability, by market order."},{"id":"parameter-3-stop","statement":"The stop distance is 2.0 times the ATR(20) of completed D1 bars, computed with the Wilder recurrence atr += (true range - atr) / 20 seeded with the first bar's high-low range as in the exploratory research, not with a 20-bar average seed, at the entry signal, set below the average entry fill; a completed H1 bar whose low reaches the stop closes the leg by a reduce-only market order on that frame. It is not a resting exchange stop order, so fills can be worse than the stop."},{"id":"parameter-4-sizing","statement":"Fixed quantities of 0.01 BTC, 0.3 ETH and 7 SOL are proposal assumptions, not the 1% risk sizing used in the exploratory research, risk parity, volatility scaling, capacity evidence, or a granted effect budget."},{"id":"parameter-5-selection","statement":"Coordinate 0 is the sole primary; coordinates 1 and 2 are nonselectable sensitivities. No lookback search, instrument expansion, result fitting, or holdout-driven replacement is admitted."}]},"revision":1,"schema_version":1}
